<div id="formulaPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('formulaPop')">Close</button><h3>Formula Sheet - SMS 3410</h3><p><b>Return:</b> R = (P1 - P0 + Dividend) / P0 | <b>Expected return:</b> E[R] = Sum p_i R_i | <b>Portfolio:</b> E[Rp] = w E[RA] + (1-w) E[RB] | <b>Variance:</b> Var[Rp] = w^2 VarA + (1-w)^2 VarB + 2w(1-w) CovAB | <b>CAPM:</b> E[Ri] = Rf + Beta_i (E[Rm] - Rf) | <b>Beta:</b> Beta = Cov(Ri,Rm) / Var(Rm) | <b>Sharpe:</b> (E[Rp] - Rf) / SDp | <b>Forward price:</b> F = S0 (1 + r)^T | <b>Put-call parity:</b> C + PV(K) = P + S0 | <b>Bond:</b> Price = Coupon x a-angle-n + Redemption x v^n</p></div>
<div id="glossPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('glossPop')">Close</button><h3>Glossary - SMS 3410</h3><p><b>Financial economics:</b> how markets price risk. <b>Asset:</b> share, bond, property. <b>Return:</b> gain from an asset. <b>Risk:</b> uncertainty of return. <b>Utility:</b> satisfaction from wealth. <b>Risk averse:</b> prefers sure thing to gamble. <b>Diversification:</b> spreading risk. <b>CAPM:</b> model linking return to market risk. <b>Beta:</b> sensitivity to market. <b>Efficient market:</b> prices reflect all information. <b>Derivative:</b> value comes from another asset. <b>Option:</b> right, not duty, to buy or sell. <b>Forward:</b> agreement to buy later at fixed price.</p></div>
