<h2>Topic 1: Introduction to Financial Economics - Markets, Assets, Players</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define financial economics, explain markets, distinguish shares, bonds, money market.</p>
<p>Financial economics asks: What should an asset cost? How do people choose between risk and return?</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Markets:</b> Money market (short-term, &lt;1 year, Treasury bills), Capital market (long-term, shares and bonds), Derivatives market (forwards, options).</p><p><b>Assets:</b> Share = part-ownership, dividend + price rise. Bond = loan to company/government, coupon + redemption. Cash = safe, low return.</p><p><b>Players:</b> Savers, borrowers, insurers, pension funds, banks, government, 【entity-NSE¦canonical_name=NSE】 (Nairobi Securities Exchange).</p><p><b>Example:</b> 【entity-Safaricom¦canonical_name=Safaricom】 share at 15, dividend 1. Return if price rises to 17 = (17-15+1)/15 = 20%.</p></div>
