<h2>Topic 3: CAPM and Factor Models</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain CAPM, calculate expected return, interpret beta, explain factor models.</p>
<p>CAPM says: Return = Risk-free rate + Beta x Market risk premium. Only market risk is rewarded, because other risk can be diversified away.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>CAPM:</b> E[Ri] = Rf + Beta_i (E[Rm] - Rf).</p><p><b>Beta:</b> Beta = Cov(Ri,Rm) / Var(Rm). Beta 1.0 = moves with market. Beta 1.5 = moves 1.5x market. Beta 0.5 = moves half market. Beta 0 = risk-free.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Rf=8%, E[Rm]=14%, Beta=1.2. E[Ri] = 8% + 1.2 x (14%-8%) = 8% + 7.2% = 15.2%.</p><p><b>Factor models:</b> Return depends on more than market - size, value, momentum. Fama-French adds size and value factors.</p></div>
