<h2>Topic 4: Efficient Markets and Behavioural Finance</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain EMH, distinguish weak, semi-strong, strong, explain behavioural biases.</p>
<p>Efficient Market Hypothesis: Prices reflect all available information. You cannot beat the market by skill, only by luck or more risk.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Weak:</b> Prices reflect past prices. Technical analysis cannot work.</p><p><b>Semi-strong:</b> Prices reflect all public information. Fundamental analysis cannot work.</p><p><b>Strong:</b> Prices reflect all information, even insider. Nothing can work.</p><p><b>Behavioural finance:</b> People are not fully rational. Biases: Overconfidence, Herding (follow others), Loss aversion (fear loss more than love gain), Anchoring.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Herding: everyone buys a share because others buy it, price rises, then crashes.</p></div>
