<h2>Topic 5: Derivatives - Forwards, Futures, Options and Swaps</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define derivatives, explain forwards, futures, options, swaps, calculate forward price and option payoff.</p>
<p>A derivative's value comes from another asset - share, bond, currency, commodity.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Forward:</b> Agreement to buy later at price fixed today. F = S0 (1+r)^T. Example: S0=100, r=10%, T=1. F = 110.</p><p><b>Futures:</b> Like forward, but traded on exchange, daily settlement.</p><p><b>Call option:</b> Right, not duty, to BUY at strike K. Payoff = max(0, S - K). <b>Put option:</b> Right to SELL. Payoff = max(0, K - S).</p><p><b>Swap:</b> Exchange cashflows, e.g. fixed interest for floating interest.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Call, K=100, S at expiry=120. Payoff = 20. If S=90, payoff = 0.</p></div>
