<h2>Topic 6: Interest Rate Models, Bonds and Financial Economics in Insurance</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain interest rate models, value bonds, explain how financial economics applies to insurers.</p>
<p>Insurers hold billions in bonds. If interest rates move, bond prices move, and insurers gain or lose.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Bond price:</b> Price = Coupon x a-angle-n + Redemption x v^n. If yield rises, price falls.</p><p><b>Term structure:</b> Yield curve - yields for different maturities. Upward sloping = long rates higher than short rates.</p><p><b>Insurer use:</b> 1. Value liabilities - discount future claims at market rates. 2. Match assets to liabilities - duration matching. 3. Price with-profits - guarantee must be affordable. 4. Manage risk - use derivatives to hedge.</p></div>
